---
description: Keep CHANGELOG.md updated on feature branches (concise Unreleased notes)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Changelog (agents)

Every user-visible or operator-facing change on a feature branch must update root `CHANGELOG.md` before the PR.

## Where

- Add a bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in the right section: `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, or `Security`.
- Do **not** bump SemVer or move Unreleased into a versioned section (release cut only; see `docs/versioning.md`).

## Style (keep it short)

- One bullet per ticket/PR outcome — usually **one sentence**.
- Write for operators/users: what changed and why it matters, not file lists or implementation tours.
- Prefer plain language; bold a short product name only when it helps scan.
- Append `(#N)` when there is a tracking issue.
- English only (project language).

### Good

- `Per-server **Auto-start with YARK** (default off); Settings lists opted-in profiles (#53).`

### Too verbose (avoid)

- Multi-sentence walkthroughs of scheduler order, DB migrations, component splits, or test filenames.

## What's new (release cut)

`src/shared/settings/changelog.ts` is the operator What's new: in-app Settings, getyark.com, and Discord `#releases`.

- A feature operators see for the first time goes under **Highlights**. Do not file that feature, or polish that only exists because it is new, under **Changed** or **Fixed**. In root `CHANGELOG.md`, those same items go under **Added**.
- Write so an operator understands it and wants to try it. Name the screen and what they can do there. Do not explain that the feature was already on `main` or hidden in an earlier release.

## When you may skip

- Pure chore/CI/docs with **no** product or operator impact: ask for / apply the GitHub label `skip-changelog` (CI enforces this).
- CI fails the PR if the `## [Unreleased]` section of `CHANGELOG.md` is unchanged and that label is absent (`.github/workflows/changelog.yml`).
